UNIT ringLabel
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY spec
SIG ringLabel(items: array, gate) -> Promise<array of strings>
DESCRIPTION ringLabel coordinates a ring of actors who process items in sequence. Each actor i holds the token in turn and: (1) formats a string as "<i>:<items[i]>", (2) engages gate.token to obtain and relinquish the token, and (3) contributes the formatted string to the output array. The unit returns an ordered array of formatted strings, one per input item.
RING The token is obtained by actor 0 via gate.token.take(0). Each subsequent actor i (i > 0) receives it from the previous actor via gate.token.pass(i-1, i). The final actor N-1 releases it via gate.token.release(N-1).
INVARIANT The output array contains exactly N strings, where position i holds the formatted string "<i>:<items[i]>".
INVARIANT Mutual exclusion: at most one actor holds the token at any instant.
INVARIANT Exactly one take call (by actor 0), exactly N-1 pass calls (one between each adjacent pair), and exactly one release call (by actor N-1). No duplication, no loss.
INVARIANT Upon return, no actor holds the token.
INVARIANT For empty input (items has length 0), return an empty array and do not call take, pass, or release.
